      "name": "save_proposal_content",
      "description": "Save structured proposal content to an existing draft proposal. This populates the full proposal with executive summary, scope, timeline, pricing, and payment schedule — ready for review in Command Center.\n\n## Proposal Guidelines\n\nCould not load company settings. Use sensible defaults for a Singapore-based software agency.\n\n## Writing Guidelines\n\n- Executive summary should be client-facing, professional, reference the client by name, and use markdown formatting (bold for emphasis, bullet points for key highlights, clear paragraph breaks)\n- Scope modules should match what was discussed in conversation\n- Pricing must match the amounts discussed — currency amounts should be whole numbers or round to nearest 50\n- Payment schedule: 2-3 milestones unless discussed differently (e.g. 50% kickoff, 50% go-live)\n- Include realistic inclusions/exclusions\n- No buzzwords (\"leverage\", \"synergy\", \"cutting-edge\")\n\n## Client Type Awareness\n\nInfer the client type from context and adjust:\n- **Startup/Small business**: Budget-conscious, value MVP approach, suggest phased delivery\n- **SME**: Balance features with budget, highlight ROI\n- **Enterprise**: Emphasize security, compliance, scalability, SLA guarantees\n- **Government/Public sector**: Formal tone, compliance-first, structured language",
